N0REP0
### : OpamSwitchState.universe takes a requested argument. requested is a set of
### : of packages. For historical reasons, it used to build a potentially larger
### : set of packages when preparing the solver universe to determine where to
### : apply with-test and the likes and which packages to reinstall.
### : This is a costly operation and also happens to lead to potentially unwanted
### : operations.
### :
### : Here we define 2 version of a package foo. foo.1 depends on depa and foo.2
### : depends on depb.
### <pkg:depa.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
build: [["echo" "depa installed!"]]
### <pkg:depb.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
build: [["echo" "depb installed!"]]
### <pkg:foo.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depends: [ "depa" ]
### <pkg:foo.2>
opam-version: "2.0"
depends: [ "depb" ]
### OPAMYES=1
### opam switch create bar --empty
### : We install foo.1 which logically requires depa.1 to be installed
### opam install foo.1
The following actions will be performed:
=== install 2 packages
  - install depa 1 [required by foo]
  - install foo  1

<><> Processing actions <><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><>
-> installed depa.1
-> installed foo.1
Done.
### : We then update depa.1
### <pkg:depa.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
build: [["echo" "depa reinstalled!"]]
### : We can see the package is now pending reinstallation
### opam reinstall --list-pending
depa.1
### : We now install foo.2, which does not depend on depa. As expected, depa
### : is not reinstalled
### opam install foo.2
The following actions will be performed:
=== install 1 package
  - install depb 1      [required by foo]
=== upgrade 1 package
  - upgrade foo  1 to 2

<><> Processing actions <><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><>
-> removed   foo.1
-> installed depb.1
-> installed foo.2
Done.
